Vendored from plasma-desktop applets/taskmanager, branch Plasma/6.6,
commit 75d05b770f1e791b45a458719466083cf343834f.

Why: Plasma 6 stopped shipping org.kde.plasma.private.taskmanager as an
importable QML module. The taskmanager applet now registers Backend and
SmartLauncherItem into its own module (org.kde.plasma.taskmanager) which is
embedded in a qrc inside plugins/plasma/applets/org.kde.plasma.taskmanager.so
and is not on the QML import path, so Latte cannot import it.

Local changes to the upstream files:
  * QML_ELEMENT / QML_NAMED_ELEMENT removed -- Latte registers the types by
    hand in lattetasksplugin.cpp under org.kde.latte.private.tasks.
  * log_settings.{h,cpp} added as a stand-in for plasma-desktop's logging
    category, so the sources compile unmodified in that respect.
  * Backend regained members Plasma 6 dropped but Latte still uses:
      - generateMimeData(), jsonArrayToUrlList()   (from the Plasma 5 Backend)
      - highlightWindows, windowViewAvailable, windowsHovered(),
        cancelHighlightWindows(), activateWindowView()
        (re-implemented over the same KWin D-Bus interfaces the Plasma 6
         applet now calls from QML, so Latte's QML is unchanged)
  * kactivitymanagerd_plugins_settings.kcfg/.kcfgc copied in, since
    recentDocumentActions() needs the generated settings class.

Not restored: ungrabMouse(), which no longer exists in Plasma 5.27 either --
Latte's two call sites were already dead and have been removed.
